@xiaolizi0v0/dsh-web-search-serper README · Request：`POST https://google.serper.dev/search` with header `X-API-KEY` and body:

```json
{ "q": "<query>", "gl": "us", "hl": "en", "num": 10, "page": 1 }
```

`num` follows the caller's `maxResults` when that is smaller than the configured
page size. The seam enforces the final cap, so `truncated` is never set here.

@xiaolizi0v0/dsh-web-search-serper README · The plugin's own tool (`serper_search`)：`dsh-tool-web` owns the model-facing `web_search`, and that tool goes through the
seam, so it depends on provider selection. `serper_search` calls this plugin's
provider object directly, so it works without `searchProvider` being configured:

```json
{ "query": "deepseek harness", "type": "news", "page": 2, "maxResults": 5 }
```

@xiaolizi0v0/dsh-web-search-serper README · plugin_manager: action install_bundle, target <absolute path to this directory>：The seam request shape carries only `query` and `maxResults`; the extra fields the
tool passes (`block`, `page`, `gl`, `hl`) are provider-private extensions used on
the tool path only.
